## Advice

- In the ScoutDocumentation workflows (e.g. ComputerUse) and repos
(e.g. scout-ai) are different things. Use the help_workflow to get
workflow/agent documetation that agents see. Use the workflow/agent name as a
repo to see the user, developer and research documentation, if available.

- Non ComputerUse tooling should not be allowed to create arbitrary files
outside of the files_dir (aka <path>.files) sidecar dir of a job. This tooling
is not in general protected by a sandbox, like ComputerUse, so it's better save
the data as the result of the tool or in one of the files inside the files_dir
sidecar and have ComputerUse tooling copy or move it to the final destination.

- When you ask another agent for help and he returns a response, it you used
a named conversation you can continue that conversation to ask clarifications
about that response.

- When writing text consider the template below, which loads a file inside lib
whith a compatible name with the name of the test. This is compatible to the
preferred way to organize unit tests, when the unit tests are for code that is
primarily in the code file ./lib/scout/dir/file.rb, then the test file should
be ./test/scout/dir/test_file.rb, it helps coder.
